<Layout
	title="About Lumen Studio"
	description="Lumen Studio is a design agency helping brands craft meaningful digital experiences."
	pubDate={new Date('March 12 2018')}
>
	<p>
		Lumen Studio was founded in San Francisco in 2018 by creative director Maya Okafor and lead engineer Daniel Reyes. What started as a two-person consultancy working out of a co-working space on Folsom Street has grown into a team of twelve — designers, developers, strategists, and writers — united by a single belief: that great digital products are built at the intersection of craft and empathy.
	</p>

	<p>
		The name comes from the Latin word for light and the basic unit of luminous flux. We liked the double meaning. Design, at its best, illuminates — it makes the complex feel simple, the unfamiliar feel intuitive, and the overlooked feel seen. Every project we take on, we ask: what does this need to make it clearer?
	</p>

	<p>
		Over the past six years we've worked with over 60 clients across fintech, healthcare, e-commerce, SaaS, and education. Some are household names. Most aren't — and that's fine. We're drawn to problems that matter, not logos that look good in a deck. Our best work has come from clients who trust us enough to disagree with us.
	</p>

	<p>
		We run on a simple model: small teams, deep focus, honest feedback. We don't take on more than we can do well. When we're at capacity, we say so. We'd rather turn down work than do it badly.
	</p>

	<p>
		If you're curious about working together, we'd love to hear about your project. We're especially interested in work that involves complex user flows, data-heavy interfaces, or products that serve underrepresented communities. <a href="/contact">Get in touch.</a>
	</p>

	<h2>The team</h2>

	<p><strong>Maya Okafor</strong> — Creative Director. Former Design Lead at fintech startup Meridian. Studied graphic design at RISD. Believes every decision should be defensible to a user.</p>

	<p><strong>Daniel Reyes</strong> — Engineering Lead. Previously at thoughtbot and Basecamp. Obsessed with web performance and writing CSS that makes sense six months later.</p>

	<p><strong>Soo-Jin Park</strong> — UX Research Lead. PhD in human-computer interaction from Carnegie Mellon. Has run over 400 usability sessions and never gets tired of watching people use software for the first time.</p>

	<p><strong>Tom Weatherley</strong> — Brand Strategist. Spent ten years in brand consulting before deciding he liked smaller clients and fewer meetings. Writes a newsletter about design history.</p>
</Layout>
